{"answer": "{
  "summary": "Focused correction/completion of the applied CLI batch. (1) CRITICAL: bench/idma_research.c validate_fullstats_raw bounded the fullstats totals with the V-side/common registers 0xc1a..0xc1d; replaced with the actual A common-window registers C1B=win_main_A (0xc1b), C1D=win_complete_A (0xc1d), C1F=win_select_A (0xc1f), C23=win_miss_A (0xc23), each with its own error message (duration keeps the 0xc19 common-window bound). (2) tests/research_cli_stub.c: fullstats_good now carries coherent A common counters (added nonzero 0xc1f/0xc23); fill_fullstats was rewritten to key off the fullstats_ prefix, keep the good base coherent, and add targeted corruption modes for magic/version/group count/stride/header reserved/group reserved/empty group/min/max order/wide-product mean and each individual totals bound. (3) tests/board-research.sh: added the missing cost-fullstats row selection (awk -F \"$TAB\" '$4 == \"cost\"' -> 21 rows) and appends --require-fullstats to the real argv (so the .cmd and argv.tsv records match the invocation). (4) tests/test_research_cli.py: tightened the old-BIT-missing-required case to assert the targeted 'fullstats magic missing' message and added targeted assertions for every new corrupt mode. (5) tests/test_research_plan.py: added CostFullstatsPlanTest and CostFullstatsRunnerTest (all-21 selection, immutable base cases, exact short-3 + six-conditions-main-3 order, frozen TSV/hash unchanged, runner 21 exact flags/ids/ordinals and stop-on-first-failure). scripts/research_plan.py already contains FULLSTATS_MODE/FULLSTATS_CASE_COUNT and the select_cases branch, so no edit there. No hardware, RTL, driver or analyzer files touched; no tests were run by me.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "bench/idma_research.c",
      "old": "\tif (total_main > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1a] ||\n\t    total_complete > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1b] ||\n\t    total_req > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1c] ||\n\t    total_miss > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1d]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats totals exceed common window\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}\n\tif (total_duration > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc19]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats duration exceeds window\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}",
      "new": "\t/* Common-window A counters use the A (not V) registers:\n\t * 0xc1b win_main_A, 0xc1d win_complete_A, 0xc1f win_select_A and\n\t * 0xc23 win_miss_A.  0xc1a/0xc1c are V-side window counters and must\n\t * not bound the A aggregation.  Every bound fails on its own field. */\n\tif (total_main > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1b]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats total main exceeds common window main\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}\n\tif (total_complete > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1d]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats total complete exceeds common window complete\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}\n\tif (total_req > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc1f]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats total requests exceed common window select\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}\n\tif (total_miss > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc23]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats total misses exceed common window miss\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}\n\tif (total_duration > (unsigned __int128)raw[0xc19]) {\n\t\tsnprintf(err, errlen, \"fullstats duration exceeds window\");\n\t\treturn -1;\n\t}"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/research_cli_stub.c",
      "old": "\t/* Window-scoped occupancy counters are bounded by raw[0xc19]. */\n\traw[0xc1a] = 300000;\n\traw[0xc1b] = 100000;\n\traw[0xc1c] = 400000;\n\traw[0xc1d] = 150000;",
      "new": "\t/* Window-scoped counters are bounded by raw[0xc19].  0xc1a/0xc1c are\n\t * V-side window counters; 0xc1b/0xc1d are the A main/complete window\n\t * counters and 0xc1f/0xc23 the A select/miss window counters used to\n\t * bound the fullstats group totals. */\n\traw[0xc1a] = 300000;\n\traw[0xc1b] = 100000;\n\traw[0xc1c] = 400000;\n\traw[0xc1d] = 150000;\n\traw[0xc1f] = 200000;\n\traw[0xc23] = 120000;"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/research_cli_stub.c",
      "old": "static void fill_fullstats(struct idma_research *r, const char *m)\n{\n\tuint64_t *raw = (uint64_t *)(uintptr_t)r->raw_user;\n\n\tif (!raw)\n\t\treturn;\n\tif (strcmp(m, \"fullstats_good\") && strcmp(m, \"fullstats_corrupt\") &&\n\t    strcmp(m, \"fullstats_large\"))\n\t\treturn;\n\traw[0xd00] = IDMA_FULLSTATS_MAGIC;\n\traw[0xd01] = 1;\n\traw[0xd02] = 6;\n\traw[0xd03] = 16;\n\traw[0xd04] = 0;\n\tif (r->a_pages == 0) {\n\t\traw[0xd05] = 0;\n\t\traw[0xc14] = 0;\n\t\traw[0xc15] = 0;\n\t} else if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_large\")) {\n\t\traw[0xd05] = 1;\n\t\traw[0xc14] = 1;\n\t\traw[0xc15] = 0;\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 0, 1, UINT64_MAX, 1, 0, 4, 0,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 0xFFFFFFFFULL, 1, 1, 0, 0);\n\t} else {\n\t\traw[0xd05] = 16;\n\t\traw[0xc14] = 16;\n\t\traw[0xc15] = 1;\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 0, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 0,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 1, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 4,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 2, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 8,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 3, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 12,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t}\n\tif (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_corrupt\"))\n\t\traw[0xd04] = 1;\n}",
      "new": "static void fill_fullstats(struct idma_research *r, const char *m)\n{\n\tuint64_t *raw = (uint64_t *)(uintptr_t)r->raw_user;\n\tunsigned int base = 0xD10;\n\n\tif (!raw)\n\t\treturn;\n\tif (strncmp(m, \"fullstats_\", 10) != 0)\n\t\treturn;\n\traw[0xd00] = IDMA_FULLSTATS_MAGIC;\n\traw[0xd01] = 1;\n\traw[0xd02] = 6;\n\traw[0xd03] = 16;\n\traw[0xd04] = 0;\n\tif (r->a_pages == 0) {\n\t\traw[0xd05] = 0;\n\t\traw[0xc14] = 0;\n\t\traw[0xc15] = 0;\n\t} else if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_large\")) {\n\t\t/* Wide-product case: min_main * count = 2^31 * 2^33 is 2^64 and\n\t\t * wraps to 0 in 64-bit arithmetic, so a 64-bit mean check would\n\t\t * wrongly accept; the 128-bit check rejects with the mean-range\n\t\t * error.  The totals are irrelevant (the group loop fires first). */\n\t\traw[0xd05] = 16;\n\t\traw[0xc14] = 16;\n\t\traw[0xc15] = 1;\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 0, 0x200000000ULL, 1, 0, 0,\n\t\t\t\t    0x800000000ULL, 0,\n\t\t\t\t    0x80000000ULL, 0xFFFFFFFFULL,\n\t\t\t\t    0, 0, 0, 0);\n\t} else {\n\t\traw[0xd05] = 16;\n\t\traw[0xc14] = 16;\n\t\traw[0xc15] = 1;\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 0, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 0,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 1, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 4,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 2, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 8,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t\tput_fullstats_group(raw, 3, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16, 12,\n\t\t\t\t    1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2);\n\t}\n\tif (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_corrupt\"))\n\t\traw[0xd04] = 1;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_magic\"))\n\t\traw[0xd00] = 0xDEADBEEFDEADBEEFULL;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_version\"))\n\t\traw[0xd01] = 2;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_groups\"))\n\t\traw[0xd02] = 5;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_stride\"))\n\t\traw[0xd03] = 8;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_header_reserved\"))\n\t\traw[0xd07] = 1;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_group_reserved\"))\n\t\traw[base + 9] = 1;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_empty\"))\n\t\traw[base + 0] = 0;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_minmax\"))\n\t\traw[base + 6] = (3ULL << 32) | 5ULL;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_total_main\"))\n\t\traw[0xc1b] = 1;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_total_complete\"))\n\t\traw[0xc1d] = 1;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_total_req\"))\n\t\traw[0xc1f] = 1;\n\telse if (!strcmp(m, \"fullstats_total_miss\"))\n\t\traw[0xc23] = 1;\n}"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/test_research_cli.py",
      "old": "        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"fullstats_good\")\n        assert row[\"success\"] is True\n        assert row[\"validated\"] is True\n        assert row[\"raw\"][0xd00] == \"0x49444d4141474731\"\n        assert row[\"input\"][\"a_pages\"] == 8\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"0\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"fullstats_good\")\n        assert row[\"success\"] is True\n        assert row[\"raw\"][0xc14] == \"0x0000000000000000\"\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\"], mode=\"fullstats_good\")\n        assert row[\"success\"] is True\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"ok\", good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n        assert row[\"validated\"] is True\n        assert row[\"errors\"]\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\"], mode=\"fullstats_corrupt\", good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n        assert row[\"validated\"] is True\n        assert row[\"errors\"]\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"fullstats_corrupt\", good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n        assert row[\"errors\"]\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"fullstats_large\", good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n        assert row[\"errors\"]",
      "new": "        def expect_error(error_args, error_mode, needle):\n            bad_row = run(error_args, mode=error_mode, good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n            assert bad_row[\"validated\"] is True, (error_mode, bad_row)\n            assert bad_row[\"success\"] is False, (error_mode, bad_row)\n            assert any(needle in message for message in bad_row[\"errors\"]), (\n                error_mode, needle, bad_row[\"errors\"])\n            return bad_row\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"fullstats_good\")\n        assert row[\"success\"] is True\n        assert row[\"validated\"] is True\n        assert row[\"raw\"][0xd00] == \"0x49444d4141474731\"\n        assert row[\"input\"][\"a_pages\"] == 8\n        # The good record carries coherent A common-window counters: 0xc1b\n        # bounds main, 0xc1d complete and 0xc1f/0xc23 the select/miss totals.\n        assert int(row[\"raw\"][0xc1b], 16) >= 16\n        assert int(row[\"raw\"][0xc1d], 16) >= 16\n        assert int(row[\"raw\"][0xc1f], 16) >= 64\n        assert int(row[\"raw\"][0xc23], 16) >= 24\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"0\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"fullstats_good\")\n        assert row[\"success\"] is True\n        assert row[\"raw\"][0xc14] == \"0x0000000000000000\"\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\"], mode=\"fullstats_good\")\n        assert row[\"success\"] is True\n\n        # Old BIT without the fullstats magic: --require-fullstats must fail\n        # with the targeted missing-magic message, not a generic error.\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], mode=\"ok\", good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n        assert row[\"validated\"] is True\n        assert any(\"fullstats magic missing\" in message for message in row[\"errors\"]), row[\"errors\"]\n\n        row = run([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\"], mode=\"fullstats_corrupt\", good=False, calls=(\"caps\", \"run\"))\n        assert row[\"validated\"] is True\n        assert any(\"fullstats sticky error nonzero\" in message for message in row[\"errors\"]), row[\"errors\"]\n\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_corrupt\", \"fullstats sticky error nonzero\")\n        # A large-invalid record must fail on the fullstats wide-product mean\n        # check, not on an unrelated cost-window check.\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_large\", \"fullstats group mean out of range\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_magic\", \"fullstats magic unknown\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_version\", \"fullstats version mismatch\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_groups\", \"fullstats group count mismatch\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_stride\", \"fullstats group stride mismatch\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_header_reserved\", \"fullstats header reserved nonzero\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_group_reserved\", \"fullstats group reserved nonzero\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_empty\", \"fullstats empty group nonzero\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_minmax\", \"fullstats group min/max order\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_total_main\", \"fullstats total main exceeds common window\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_total_complete\", \"fullstats total complete exceeds common window\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_total_req\", \"fullstats total requests exceed common window\")\n        expect_error([\"--cost\", \"--a-pages\", \"8\", \"--require-fullstats\"], \"fullstats_total_miss\", \"fullstats total misses exceed common window\")"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/board-research.sh",
      "old": "# Select the rows this mode executes: short/all keep the historical prefix and\n# the whole plan, cost-followup is a fixed filter over the same validated\n# 84-row plan (no operator edit on the board), so the selected ids, ordinals\n# and per-block order are exactly the frozen ones and other conditions drop out.\ncase \"$MODE\" in\n    cost-followup)\n        if ! awk -F \"$TAB\" '\n            ($3 == \"short\" && $4 == \"cost\" && ($1 == \"short-cost-solo\" || $1 == \"short-cost-a8g0\")) ||\n            ($3 == \"main\" && $4 == \"cost\" && ($5 == \"solo\" || $5 == \"a8g0\" || $5 == \"a8g2000\"))\n        ' \"$OUT/plan.data.tsv\" > \"$OUT/plan.selected.tsv\"; then\n            fatal \"plan selection failed\"\n        fi\n        ;;\n    *)\n        if ! sed -n \"1,${SEL_N}p\" \"$OUT/plan.data.tsv\" > \"$OUT/plan.selected.tsv\"; then\n            fatal \"plan selection failed\"\n        fi\n        ;;\nesac",
      "new": "# Select the rows this mode executes: short/all keep the historical prefix and\n# the whole plan, cost-followup is a fixed filter over the same validated\n# 84-row plan (no operator edit on the board), so the selected ids, ordinals\n# and per-block order are exactly the frozen ones and other conditions drop out.\n# cost-fullstats is a pure filter that keeps every cost row ($4 == \"cost\"):\n# the 3 short-stage cost cases plus the 18 main-stage cost cases, in frozen\n# order, exactly the 21 rows the full-aggregation segment expects.\ncase \"$MODE\" in\n    cost-followup)\n        if ! awk -F \"$TAB\" '\n            ($3 == \"short\" && $4 == \"cost\" && ($1 == \"short-cost-solo\" || $1 == \"short-cost-a8g0\")) ||\n            ($3 == \"main\" && $4 == \"cost\" && ($5 == \"solo\" || $5 == \"a8g0\" || $5 == \"a8g2000\"))\n        ' \"$OUT/plan.data.tsv\" > \"$OUT/plan.selected.tsv\"; then\n            fatal \"plan selection failed\"\n        fi\n        ;;\n    cost-fullstats)\n        if ! awk -F \"$TAB\" '$4 == \"cost\"' \"$OUT/plan.data.tsv\" > \"$OUT/plan.selected.tsv\"; then\n            fatal \"plan selection failed\"\n        fi\n        ;;\n    *)\n        if ! sed -n \"1,${SEL_N}p\" \"$OUT/plan.data.tsv\" > \"$OUT/plan.selected.tsv\"; then\n            fatal \"plan selection failed\"\n        fi\n        ;;\nesac"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/board-research.sh",
      "old": "    case \"$c_mode\" in\n        e2)\n            case_args=\"--e2 --a-pages $c_apages --a-transfers $c_acount --window-cycles $c_window --warmup $c_warmup --timeout-ms $c_timeout\"\n            ;;\n        cost)\n            # Cost mode has no A-transfer count: the A (P4M) batch runs until V\n            # finishes and is then stopped/drained, so no --a-transfers is passed.\n            case_args=\"--cost --a-pages $c_apages --a-gap-cycles $c_gap --transfers $c_vcount --warmup $c_warmup --timeout-ms $c_timeout\"\n            ;;\n        *)\n            stop 2 \"selected_line_bad_mode id=$c_id mode=$c_mode\"\n            ;;\n    esac",
      "new": "    case \"$c_mode\" in\n        e2)\n            case_args=\"--e2 --a-pages $c_apages --a-transfers $c_acount --window-cycles $c_window --warmup $c_warmup --timeout-ms $c_timeout\"\n            ;;\n        cost)\n            # Cost mode has no A-transfer count: the A (P4M) batch runs until V\n            # finishes and is then stopped/drained, so no --a-transfers is passed.\n            case_args=\"--cost --a-pages $c_apages --a-gap-cycles $c_gap --transfers $c_vcount --warmup $c_warmup --timeout-ms $c_timeout\"\n            # cost-fullstats requires the full-aggregation raw fields; the flag\n            # is appended to the real invocation, so the recorded .cmd file and\n            # the argv.tsv row match it exactly.\n            if [ \"$MODE\" = \"cost-fullstats\" ]; then\n                case_args=\"$case_args --require-fullstats\"\n            fi\n            ;;\n        *)\n            stop 2 \"selected_line_bad_mode id=$c_id mode=$c_mode\"\n            ;;\n    esac"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/test_research_plan.py",
      "old": "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()",
      "new": "FULLSTATS_IDS = (\n    \"short-cost-solo\",\n    \"short-cost-a8g0\",\n    \"short-cost-a16g0\",\n    \"cost-b01-solo\",\n    \"cost-b01-a1g0\",\n    \"cost-b01-a8g0\",\n    \"cost-b01-a16g0\",\n    \"cost-b01-a8g1000\",\n    \"cost-b01-a8g2000\",\n    \"cost-b02-a1g0\",\n    \"cost-b02-a8g0\",\n    \"cost-b02-a16g0\",\n    \"cost-b02-a8g1000\",\n    \"cost-b02-a8g2000\",\n    \"cost-b02-solo\",\n    \"cost-b03-a8g0\",\n    \"cost-b03-a16g0\",\n    \"cost-b03-a8g1000\",\n    \"cost-b03-a8g2000\",\n    \"cost-b03-solo\",\n    \"cost-b03-a1g0\",\n)\nFULLSTATS_ORDINALS = (\n    4, 5, 6, 67, 68, 69, 70, 71, 72, 73, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 82, 83, 84,\n)\n\n\nclass CostFullstatsPlanTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    \"\"\"The fixed cost-fullstats selection of the frozen 84-case plan.\n\n    Host-side only.  Appended as an independent class so the frozen short/all\n    expectations and build_plan() stay untouched.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def test_selection_is_exactly_the_twenty_one_cost_cases(self):\n        plan = research_plan.build_plan()\n        selected = research_plan.select_cases(\n            plan[\"cases\"], research_plan.FULLSTATS_MODE\n        )\n        self.assertEqual(len(selected), 21)\n        self.assertEqual(research_plan.FULLSTATS_CASE_COUNT, 21)\n        self.assertEqual([c[\"id\"] for c in selected], list(FULLSTATS_IDS))\n        self.assertEqual([c[\"ordinal\"] for c in selected], list(FULLSTATS_ORDINALS))\n        self.assertEqual([c[\"mode\"] for c in selected], [\"cost\"] * 21)\n        self.assertEqual(\n            [c[\"stage\"] for c in selected], [\"short\"] * 3 + [\"main\"] * 18\n        )\n\n    def test_selection_returns_flag_copies_and_leaves_base_cases_immutable(self):\n        plan = research_plan.build_plan()\n        base = plan[\"cases\"]\n        before = [\n            {key: (list(value) if key == \"argv\" else value) for key, value in case.items()}\n            for case in base\n        ]\n        selected = research_plan.select_cases(base, research_plan.FULLSTATS_MODE)\n        originals = {c[\"id\"]: c for c in base}\n        for case in selected:\n            self.assertIs(case.get(\"require_fullstats\"), True)\n            self.assertEqual(case[\"argv\"][-1], \"--require-fullstats\")\n            self.assertIsNot(case, originals[case[\"id\"]])\n        # The base frozen cases are untouched: no flag, no require_fullstats.\n        self.assertNotIn(\"require_fullstats\", base[3])\n        self.assertEqual(base[3][\"argv\"][-1], \"10000\")\n        after = [\n            {key: (list(value) if key == \"argv\" else value) for key, value in case.items()}\n            for case in base\n        ]\n        self.assertEqual(before, after)\n\n    def test_short_three_and_six_conditions_main_three(self):\n        plan = research_plan.build_plan()\n        selected = research_plan.select_cases(\n            plan[\"cases\"], research_plan.FULLSTATS_MODE\n        )\n        short = [c for c in selected if c[\"stage\"] == \"short\"]\n        self.assertEqual(\n            [c[\"id\"] for c in short],\n            [\"short-cost-solo\", \"short-cost-a8g0\", \"short-cost-a16g0\"],\n        )\n        main = [c for c in selected if c[\"stage\"] == \"main\"]\n        self.assertEqual(len(main), 18)\n        for condition in research_plan.COST_CONDITIONS:\n            self.assertEqual(\n                sum(1 for c in main if c[\"condition\"] == condition), 3\n            )\n        for block in (1, 2, 3):\n            order = list(research_plan.rotate(research_plan.COST_CONDITIONS, block))\n            chunk = main[(block - 1) * 6:block * 6]\n            self.assertEqual([c[\"condition\"] for c in chunk], order)\n            self.assertEqual([c[\"block\"] for c in chunk], [block] * 6)\n\n    def test_frozen_tsv_and_generator_hash_are_unchanged(self):\n        plan = research_plan.build_plan()\n        text = research_plan.to_tsv(plan)\n        self.assertEqual(text, FROZEN_TSV.read_text(encoding=\"